# Git workflow (hermes-stack)

Follow **[docs/GIT.md](../../docs/GIT.md)** as the source of truth.

## Core rule

- `develop` = everything integrating / testing
- `main` = production-ready only
- `release/*` = selected features for the next production cut

```text
feature/* ──MR──> develop ──> release/* ──MR──> main
```

## Branches

| Branch | From | MR into |
|--------|------|---------|
| `feature/*` | `develop` | `develop` |
| `fix/*` | `develop` | `develop` |
| `hotfix/*` | `main` | `main` (+ sync `develop`) |
| `release/vX.Y.Z` | `main`, then cherry-pick ready features | `main` |

## MR title (required)

```text
[TYPE][LAYER] Imperative summary
[RELEASE] Release vX.Y.Z
```

Examples: `[FEATURE][MEMORY] Add memory manager` · `[FIX][SESSION] Fix session isolation` · `[RELEASE] Release v1.5.0`

## Must

- Update `docs/CHANGELOG.md` (top + timestamp) for ops/product changes
- Do not merge untested 🧪 features into `release/*` / `main`
- Push only when GitHub auth is the repo owner (`7ringuy4n` for this repo)
- No VPS/remote apply without explicit permission
- Force-push / amend only when the operator explicitly asks (`--force-with-lease`)
- Do not commit `.env`, secrets, or `scripts/temp/**` / `hermes/temp/**` drafts
